  "goodToKnow": "Die Luftfeuchtigkeit is humidity: hohe Luftfeuchtigkeit, relative Luftfeuchtigkeit. Germans are told to keep indoor humidity around 40 to 60 percent to avoid Schimmel (mould), and tenants are expected to air rooms by Stoßlüften: opening windows wide for a few minutes several times a day, rather than leaving them tilted (gekippt). Mould is a classic landlord-tenant dispute. It has no plural."
